      "latency_ms": 5107.4,
      "prompt_tokens": 25,
      "completion_tokens": 1001,
      "output": "\n\nWater is a chemical substance composed of two hydrogen atoms and one oxygen atom, forming the molecule **H₂O**. It is a fundamental and ubiquitous substance on Earth, essential for all known forms of life. Here's a breakdown of its key characteristics:\n\n### **Chemical Composition**\n- **Molecular Structure**: Water is a polar molecule, with oxygen (more electronegative) pulling electrons toward itself, creating a partial negative charge on the oxygen and partial positive charges on the hydrogens. This polarity enables unique properties like hydrogen bonding.\n\n### **Physical Properties**\n- **States of Matter**: Water exists as a **liquid** at room temperature, but it can also freeze into a **solid (ice)** or evaporate into a **gas (water vapor)**.\n- **Unique Properties**:\n  - **High Specific Heat**: It absorbs and releases heat slowly, helping regulate temperature in organisms and environments.\n  - **Cohesion & Adhesion**: Molecules stick to each other (cohesion) and to other surfaces (adhesion), enabling processes like capillary action in plants.\n  - **Solvent Ability**: Often called the \"universal solvent,\" it dissolves many substances, facilitating chemical reactions in living systems.\n\n### **Biological Importance**\n- **Life-Sustaining**: Water is a primary component of cells, blood, and bodily fluids. It transports nutrients, removes waste, and participates in metabolic reactions.\n- **Temperature Regulation**: Through sweating and respiration, it helps maintain body temperature.\n\n### **Environmental Role**\n- **Hydrological Cycle**: Water cycles through evaporation, condensation, precipitation, and runoff, shaping Earth's climate and ecosystems.\n- **Erosion & Landscaping**: It carves rivers, lakes, and canyons over time, influencing geological features.\n\n### **Other Characteristics**\n- **Tasteless, Odorless, and Colorless**: Pure water has no taste or smell. In large quantities, it appears blue due to light absorption and scattering.\n- **Universal Solvent**: While not a perfect solvent, it dissolves more substances than any other liquid, making it critical for chemical and biological processes.\n\nIn summary, water is a simple yet extraordinary molecule whose unique properties make it indispensable for life, environmental stability, and countless natural and industrial processes."
